From: Tenda AC8 OpenWrt port
Subject: mips: rtl8197f: select HAVE_PCI and PCI_DRIVERS_GENERIC

The RTL8197F has a PCIe root complex (the external 5 GHz radio of most
boards sits on it) and the target ships a native host driver for it
(PCIE_RTL8197F), but nothing selected HAVE_PCI: CONFIG_PCI=y from the
target config was dropped, the host driver was never built and the PCI
calls of the Wi-Fi driver compiled to the !CONFIG_PCI stubs.  The host
driver uses the generic host bridge API, like the MT7621 does.
---
--- a/arch/mips/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/Kconfig
@@ -980,6 +980,8 @@
 	select CSRC_R4K
 	select CPU_SUPPORTS_CPUFREQ
 	select SYS_SUPPORTS_LITTLE_ENDIAN
+	select HAVE_PCI
+	select PCI_DRIVERS_GENERIC
 
 config RTL838X
 	bool "Realtek RTL838X based platforms"
